  "adapted": "The national seasonally adjusted annual rate is the published value multiplied by 1,000, because the Web Data Service reports that series with a scalar factor of thousands. The month-to-month changes are the differences of those published figures. Actual census metropolitan area starts are the published unit counts. Ottawa-Gatineau provincial parts are omitted because the starts table also publishes the combined census metropolitan area. The national rate covers centres of 10,000 and over; it is not an all-areas rate and it is not the sum of the census metropolitan area rows.",
